v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1-rc was healthy only in staging, so I didn't use it. After the rollback, the service reports healthy on v2.3.0 in all regions with an error rate of 0.2%. Next step: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying it.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 15201, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Msoz4cySQe9SfbUhXVwjHS", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 15201, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Msoz4cySQe9SfbUhXVwjHS", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 18473, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident, which paged on-call.\n\n- **What was wrong:** after v2.3.1 was deployed, checkout-api failed health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with 18% of requests erroring.\n- **Version I picked:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1-rc was healthy, but only in staging, so I didn't use it.\n- **Result:** all three regions are now on v2.3.0, health checks pass and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure and the rollback. It notes that the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before v2.3.1 is deployed again.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01LQbsoji38FWhuTLDjHuP5c", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_011Cof7GqrD6DnSYJjSAu8oi", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Latest healthy production release is v2.3.0 (v2.3.1-rc was only healthy in staging, so it doesn't qualify).", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_016h4XtYmUAms14dg9V9AvdF", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014ub7X6MVU8MFLE1nfGxKE7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01X77UaP95b7dGMWpLCJkpus", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Msoz4cySQe9SfbUhXVwjHS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After checkout-api v2.3.1 was deployed to production, the service failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of 18%. I rolled it back in all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1-rc was healthy only in staging, so I didn't use it. After the rollback, the service reports healthy on v2.3.0 in all regions with an error rate of 0.2%. Next step: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying it.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident, which paged on-call.\n\n- **What was wrong:** after v2.3.1 was deployed, checkout-api failed health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with 18% of requests erroring.\n- **Version I picked:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1-rc was healthy, but only in staging, so I didn't use it.\n- **Result:** all three regions are now on v2.3.0, health checks pass and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure and the rollback. It notes that the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before v2.3.1 is deployed again.", "type": "text"}]}]}